From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: damnbitimcrit <333091414+damnbitimcrit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [HID] Mouse lock with raw motion, mouse button/wheel
 bindings, analog keys

- mouse_lock (Windows): clicking into the window hides the cursor, pins it to
  the client area and forwards raw relative motion (WM_INPUT) to input
  listeners through the new OnRawMouseMove. Switching windows releases it.
  While it is on, Escape and double-click no longer leave or toggle
  fullscreen; they are game input.
- While the mouse is locked, the keyboard driver takes priority over
  controllers for keyboard_user_index (InputDriver::TakesPriority), so a
  connected gamepad doesn't take over the keyboard and mouse player.
- Keyboard bindings accept mouse buttons (VK 0x01, 0x02, 0x04, 0x05, 0x06)
  and the wheel as momentary keys 0x0A (up) and 0x0B (down).
- Bindings are re-parsed when their cvars change, so per-game config
  bindings take effect.
- keyboard_analog_movement: with the Wooting Analog SDK installed, the left
  stick follows how far its bound keys are pressed.
- hid::MouseInput collects raw motion for title code that implements mouse
  aiming.
